text='''# Independent supervisor source review

Verdict: changes required before execution. All 19 producer/source binding hashes match. This review inspected source and frozen plans only; it launched no Docker client, container, cloud command, or reviewed executable. Reviewer previously prepared runtime-route inspection/compiler-prerequisite evidence, not this supervisor.

'''
for f in findings:text+=f"{f['id']} — {f['title']} (supervise.py {f['lines']}). {f['impact']} Required correction: {f['action']}\n\n"
text+='''The prestart PID gap is accurately disclosed. Daemon PidsLimit support and HostConfig.PidsLimit=1 establish configuration/support; an opportunistic after-start cgroup read cannot establish effective enforcement before start. qualification_complete and effective_before_start_proved stay false, with exit3 on otherwise successful checks. This is appropriate partial-status reporting, not closure of the retained qualification gate.

Q0 broadens the retained explicit-member read to a bounded full /opt tar with an exact allowlist. This is a prospective scope addition, not an already executed allowance. It rejects unexpected members and never extracts archive paths. A base-image /opt extra or oversized tree can make this fail closed; no compatibility was observed. It covers /opt ancestry, not /usr/local/bin ancestry.

Positive source observations: immutable image ID and Docker client digest, env-i explicit local socket route, pull=never, unique container label/name/ID/image matching, one-container ownership, exact-ID removal and retained cleanup-incomplete status. Root supplies independently reviewed final-build joins; the supervisor only checks hash shapes and embedded build-info equality and is not a build-receipt verifier. Scientific admission remains false. Owner exit125 matches the retained early digest-rejection contract.

Timeouts are orchestration limits, not guaranteed daemon termination. The shared300second deadline,30second cleanup reserve and20second active deadline are explicit. Filesystem stalls, signal interruption and daemon behavior still need the corrected cleanup design and future bounded validation. A further receipt hardening item: outer fallback at lines193–196 labels docker_actions_started=false unconditionally; after a final receipt-write failure this should instead use tracked action state or unknown.

Producer is preparing an additive revision after receiving findings R1–R6. This review preserves v1 and does not approve unseen changes. No test execution or repair occurred. The new version needs fresh source review and separate prospective admission.
'''
(D/'REVIEW.md').write_text(text)
